  <paragraphs>
    <title>Classification version: Step functions</title>
    <p>
      <md>
        \Pr(y_i&gt;250 \mid x_i) =
        \frac{\exp(\beta_0+\beta_1C_1(x_i)+\beta_2C_2(x_i)+\cdots+\beta_KC_K(x_i))}
        {1+\exp(\beta_0+\beta_1C_1(x_i)+\beta_2C_2(x_i)+\cdots+\beta_KC_K(x_i))}
      </md>
    </p>
    <sidebyside widths="43.75% 56.25%">
      <stack>
        <image source="figures/Fig7-2b.png">
          <shortdescription>Plot showing the probability of high wage versus age using a green step function fit with dashed confidence bands.</shortdescription>
        </image>
      </stack>
      <stack>
        <p>
          <ul>
            <li><p>Again, the model learns that middle region.</p></li>
            <li><p>The confidence interval is still large on the right, likely because there is less data there.</p></li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </stack>
    </sidebyside>
  </paragraphs>

